BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:🚧 Lioness line: Willesden Junction to Harrow & Wealdstone
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261207
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
UID:77c0cd02d3559a1b62c3@tfl-closures
CATEGORIES:Part of the line closed
DESCRIPTION:🚧 Part of the line closed\n\nWillesden Junction to Harrow &
  Wealdstone\nDates as listed by TfL: Sunday 6 December 2026\n\nTfL live st
 atus (Reduced Service\, checked 24 November 2026): LIONESS LINE: Sunday 6 
 December\, a reduced service will operate between Euston and South Hampste
 ad\, and the 2359 last train from Euston to Willesden Junction will not ru
 n.\nTfL live status (Reduced Service\, checked 24 November 2026): LIONESS 
 LINE: Sunday 6 December\, a reduced service operates between Harrow & Weal
 dstone and Watford Junction.\nTfL live status (Part Closure\, checked 24 N
 ovember 2026): LIONESS LINE: Sunday 6 December\, no service between Willes
 den Junction and Harrow & Wealdstone. There will also be no BAKERLOO LINE 
 service between Queens Park and Harrow & Wealdstone. Special bus service 7
 18 operates. LONDON NORTH WESTERN RAILWAY trains continue to stop at Harro
 w & Wealdstone. SOUTHERN trains stop at Wembley Central and Harrow & Weald
 stone between 1300 and 2000 only\n\nSource: TfL planned track closures\, c
 orrect at Monday 16 November 2026. https://tfl.gov.uk/api/document/planned
 trackclosures.pdf?id=accc98cf-e761-47b3-a43b-3de08a097b8f&type=document\nP
 lans can change. Check before you travel: https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-dlr-over
 ground/status/\nPowered by TfL Open Data\nUnofficial calendar\, not produc
 ed or endorsed by Transport for London.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-dlr-overground/status/
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
